plc@vax5.cit.cornell.edu writes:
>How about this for unfair ways to die...
>-You are blinded by a flash of light (more)-
>_You try to feel what is lying on the floor (more)-
>-Touching the dead cockatrice was a fatal mistake-

The idea that a blind person can, in the same fraction of a turn as a
sighted person, classify all objects lying in the square just entered
is an interesting one, and may compensate for some less playable
aspects of blindness.  However, the idea is unrealistic, and in some
circumstances it makes the game unplayable.  Even the @-command does
not seem to prevent the player from walking around with his hands on
the floor in some situations.  This aspect of blindness may be worth
rethinking.  If the current feature is desirable, a reasonable
modification would be something like

Your foot bumped something/a thing or two/a pile of objects/.
Pick them up, feel around on the floor to classify, or ignore [pfi]?

Opinions?
